1 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073991 #edb/ref 1045 "Distances Between Points in the Coordinate Plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073991 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186074901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073991 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073991 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073991 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "71a6f31c-0bb8-5061-8779-9e3b7984d66e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074465 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186073028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074465 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61224" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074465 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074465 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the distance between the points $(4,2)$  and $(4,8)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074465 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3943d606-fff6-5e9c-a446-2d4378743487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074465 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/66/66c988b7fede0e97eae46388dd0e57aee2c49a3c185c9a888277da8fefc947ab.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $6$ units, so the distance equals $6.$\n\n![](images/63/63f70c20c918dae51ecddc7891a8cbee7c5749720521e62fe26e9bc4e33bb9e6.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/d3/d3693b8c3d07636143b2c77c3bd2645015885b77ec4e8ddffde2e121da0511bc.png)\n\nThe point $(4,8)$ is at a distance of $8$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(4,2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $8-2=6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074898 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074898 #edb/ref 1061 8890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074898 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "123d2929-5563-5b7e-8588-e7734bb4eb42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074898 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074899 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074899 #edb/ref 1061 8891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074899 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f954535e-e2c6-5a01-85b8-f90fdccafc1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074899 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074900 #edb/ref 1061 8892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074900 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a335606-3bdb-5535-8956-9a3ababd7eb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074900 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074901 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074901 #edb/ref 1061 8895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074901 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1961bdcc-cea7-5d78-88c1-4f69e1dab833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074901 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074902 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074902 #edb/ref 1061 8947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074902 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d97c5e30-e125-5cba-9973-1e1898eca20e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074902 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074978 #edb/ref 1064 "The distance between two points in the coordinate plane is the number of units between them. Let's explore two methods for calculating the horizontal distance between two points with the points $(1,1)$ and $(5,1).$\n\n**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFirst, we plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/19/196c50295e8d8a95084c31226fb9319ede7b70603d894b6939e4615df583c29c.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $4$ units, so the distance equals $4.$\n\n![](images/4b/4b531e29616f3e8d7ea0c65761e59cfea224b9c0e756c68b7647c7271dc09493.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/6d/6d5c6760e15098dc381e639cd806b6410f2fa6d9049d11d5467427635c9872b6.png)\n\nThe point $({\\color{blue}{1}},1)$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{1}$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $({\\color{red}{5}},1)$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{5}$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is ${\\color{red}{5}} - {\\color{blue}{1}} = 4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074978 #edb/ref 1065 2199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074978 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "aeee8d0d-20f6-5700-8c35-c66e0eef8daa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074978 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074979 #edb/ref 1064 "When we want to find the distance between two points in different quadrants, method 1 works exactly the same, but method 2 is slightly different.\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis for a horizontal distance, or $x$-axis for a vertical distance, and then *adding*. \n\nSo, what's the distance between $(-3,2)$ and $(1,2)?$\n\n**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/e0/e0fec8fca43b421b62efc3d6d892563c80beaab3c2816be47aa7563868555268.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $4$ units, so the distance equals $4.$\n\n![](images/dd/ddc1e6cec323fe245ff2a115a587e773d408dc0115ba5002c02ac1d238620c63.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/0b/0bbb91fc8c0e7ad577261dcdbc8e7aaa16a44e8be2e937e2d6870aae58af4ccf.png)\n\nThe point $({\\color{blue}{1}},2)$ is at a distance of $\\color{blue}{1}$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $({\\color{red}{-3}},2)$ is at a distance of $\\color{red}{3}$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is ${\\color{red}{3}} + {\\color{blue}{1}} = 4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074979 #edb/ref 1065 2204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074979 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a1233efd-87e1-5707-9b70-24c24ed47418" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074979 #edb/ref 1067 "The Distance Between Two Points in Different Quadrants" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494305 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494305 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494305 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494305 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494305 #edb/ref 1045 "Distances Between Points in the Coordinate Plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494305 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186495267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494305 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494305 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494305 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "4ad6406f-28ca-5b57-94e6-4b4cc6fef04e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494453 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494453 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494453 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "42efa052-c9ab-54d8-9f6d-f34afac5ba39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494463 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494463 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494463 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4844ffa7-9148-54b8-9e72-b30c1cb0c11e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494506 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494506 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494506 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5bdc2701-e79a-5b33-86a6-ef27722a55d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494526 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref