527091 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527091 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186526516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527091 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ba2c0b6c-0868-582f-9fb0-8f7239a4a7d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527128 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527128 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60606" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527128 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527128 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/84/84da1d1bb056c8c5d823a585889699e3ba3fe5ca7b2706b4e0a16c96f2e65ac3.png)\n\nWhat is the distance between the points $(3,1)$  and $(3,4)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527128 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0a27d18e-df05-520d-948c-41b1732464a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527128 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $3$ units, so the distance equals $3.$\n\n![](images/a0/a0eb36fd37d73ed20e0ee17717f80cb33a56910cc57eb181897ad44197a7f268.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](images/2b/2b4771270aec2dd62828f4063262cfaf81fba31f6be6d1a2ba8bfe0d59778b48.png)\n\nThe point $(3,4)$ is at a distance of $4$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(3,1)$ is at a distance of $1$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $4-1=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527153 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527153 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61265" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527153 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527153 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the distance between the points $(-3,2)$  and $(-3,-4)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527153 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ab19b4a-4627-54ee-8e9e-8d051f6ac141" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527153 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](images/c0/c0dcef8b6c0c63e17fc9b516e3e3176f054dd0eddb93c71375a3de3272da9623.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $6$ units, so the distance equals $6.$\n\n![](images/c1/c1764499f4600d5c74c598b205e0a1971ca91231c4464f77e0809a680003bf11.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/5b/5b4c4c665b07575604dc873703517548404d7c31e8395070642ca37584c6d08f.png)\n\nThe point $(-3,2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(-3,-4)$ is at a distance of $4$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $4+2=6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527168 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527168 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61105" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527168 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527168 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/25/25e1891ce31fa7043723b2dcb4cd1e01c41dbd82ae70ef5024c64ed2d6deab33.png)\n\nWhat is the distance between the points $(-3,1)$  and $(-3,-5)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527168 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "67699b33-3e46-5c7c-ad2b-2f6df6bd8eb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527168 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $6$ units, so the distance equals $6.$\n\n![](images/1f/1f3eeede9aa301cf6d64b48cc86f770fc86517ed51285da9bdc86e5a580b243f.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/a5/a504ca22769a377cd7e23e0b6a09595d00c8ad25733f3d1e6a716b52f262e139.png)\n\nThe point $(-3,-5)$ is at a distance of $5$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(-3,1)$ is at a distance of $1$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $5+1=6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527232 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186527255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527232 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12252c44-f6ed-5a4c-877a-529ad585fdea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527232 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186527128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527243 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "35f258ab-51ea-5cc4-ab06-dadec569e07a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527243 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186527153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527255 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186527287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527255 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5c465ab7-ebb0-5979-8fd6-300e20ddd25b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527255 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186527168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527287 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186527243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527287 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f27b2fa2-b4cf-5259-af6d-f395c41888da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527287 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074465 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
